title: Toggling of Configured MCP Server Availability - Implementation Tasks
status: draft
created: 2026-09-26
author: Luke Carrier
items[8]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,[x] Add enabled state tracking to McpPool,"Add enabled: BTreeMap<String, bool> field to McpPool struct and initialize all configured servers as enabled: true in constructor","McpPool struct has enabled field, all servers initialized as enabled",low,"2h",,"FR-001,FR-002,FR-003,FR-004"
  T-002,[x] Modify McpPool connection logic,"Update McpPool::connect method to skip servers where enabled.get(server) == Some(false)","McpPool::connect respects enabled state and skips disabled servers",low,"1h",T-001,"FR-001,FR-002"
  T-003,[x] Add public toggle methods to McpPool,"Implement McpPool::enable_server, disable_server, is_enabled, and toggle_server methods","All public methods compile and function correctly",medium,"3h",T-001,"FR-001,FR-002,FR-003,FR-004"
  T-004,[x] Handle connection lifecycle on toggle,"When disabling a server with active connection: close the connection; when enabling a previously connected server: attempt reconnection","Disabling closes existing connections, enabling attempts reconnection",medium,"2h",T-003,"FR-001,FR-002,FR-004"
  T-005,[x] Update McpPool status reporting,"Modify McpPool::statuses method to include enabled/disabled state in returned status","Status reporting includes enabled/disabled information alongside connection status",low,"1h",T-003,"FR-003"
  T-006,[x] Add ACP command handler detection,"In acp::run_agent_over PromptRequest handler, add condition to detect /mcp slash commands","PromptRequest handler correctly identifies /mcp commands",low,"1h",,"FR-001,FR-002,FR-003"
  T-007,[x] Implement ACP /mcp disable command,"Handle /mcp disable <server> by calling mcp_pool.disable_server(server) and returning appropriate response","/mcp disable command works and returns success/error messages",medium,"2h",T-006,"FR-001"
  T-008,[x] Implement ACP /mcp enable and status commands,"Handle /mcp enable <server> and /mcp status [<server-id>] by calling appropriate McpPool methods","/mcp enable and status commands work correctly",medium,"2h",T-006,"FR-002,FR-003"